  [in-code [#
[not true]
#]]
  [out-text [#
false
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [; ── P5. coming from Python: remark (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-remark-wrong level=core
  [title [#A `;` remark after code#]]
  [tags comment remark python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
`;` does not start a comment. Outside a bracket each bare word is a
top-level form of the program, so the "remark" runs as three more results —
`;` itself (printed `';'`), then `the`, then `sum` — after the one you meant. CX has a
line comment `# …` to the end of the line and a block comment `[; … ]`;
the raw-text block is TEXT, not a comment.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[r total=[+ 1 2]] ; the sum
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r total=3]
';'
the
sum
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-remark-right level=core
  [title [#A block comment `[; … ]`, or a line comment `# …`#]]
  [tags comment remark python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[r total=[+ 1 2]] [; the sum ]  # or a line comment
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r total=3]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [; ── P6. coming from Python: reassign (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-reassign-wrong level=core
  [title [#`[= $count …]` read as reassignment#]]
  [tags binding immutable fold loop reduce python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
`[= $x V]` is a BINDING CLAUSE, never an assignment: bindings are immutable,
and a clause inside `[?for]` binds a fresh `$count` for that one iteration,
shadowing the outer `0`. So the running total Python's `count += x` builds
(1, 3, 6) never accumulates — each pass answers `0 + x`. Carried state is a
fold: `[?reduce]` with an accumulator, or `[?loop]`, whose `[continue …]`
rebinds its declared bindings positionally for the next pass.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $count 0]
  [?for [in $x (1, 2, 3)]
    [= $count [+ $count $x]]
    [yield $count]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
1
2
3
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-reassign-right level=core
  [title [#Fold with `[?reduce]`, or carry state through `[?loop]`#]]
  [tags binding immutable fold loop reduce python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[total
  fold=[?reduce (1, 2, 3) [using [?fn ($acc $x) [+ $acc $x]]] [init 0]]
  loop=[?loop [= $i 1] [= $count 0]
         [?if [> $i 3] [then [break $count]]
           [else [continue [+ $i 1] [+ $count $i]]]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[total fold=6 loop=6]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [; ── P7. coming from Python: let-two-bodies (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-let-two-bodies-wrong level=core
  [title [#Two body forms in one `[?let]`#]]
  [tags let body sequence do python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
A `[?let]` is bindings, then exactly ONE body — the value it answers.
There is no statement list: a second form is not "the next line", so the
clause before the last is read as a malformed binding and refused. Build one
value that holds both results; to run effects in order, put them in one
`[?do A B]` (it answers `null`, and the first `[err]` stops the sequence).
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $a 2]
  [first [* $a 10]]
  [second [+ $a 1]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
error: cx-err:CXER0112: [?let] expected [= $x V] binding clause before the body at line 1:1
#]]
  [exit-code [#1#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-let-two-bodies-right level=core
  [title [#One body — one value holding both results#]]
  [tags let body sequence do python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $a 2]
  [pair
    [first [* $a 10]]
    [second [+ $a 1]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[pair [first 20] [second 3]]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [; ── P8. coming from Python: array-commas (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-array-commas-wrong level=core
  [title [#Array items without commas — `['eggs' 'peanuts']`#]]
  [tags array sequence literal comma python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
Array `[a, b]` and sequence `(a, b)` literals separate their items with
commas. Without them `['eggs' 'peanuts']` is not a two-item array; the parse
refuses at the second item.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $allergens ['eggs' 'peanuts']] [$count $allergens]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
error: cx-err:CXER0100: parse: expected ']', got peanuts at line 1:29
#]]
  [exit-code [#1#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-array-commas-right level=core
  [title [#Commas between the items — `['eggs', 'peanuts']`#]]
  [tags array sequence literal comma python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $allergens ['eggs', 'peanuts']] [$count $allergens]]
#]]
