 ]

 [; ── P17. coming from Python: string-length (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-string-length-wrong level=core
  [title [#`strings:count` (or `$count`) for a string's length#]]
  [tags strings length count python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
`strings:count` counts the occurrences of a NEEDLE (`'a'` in `'banana'` is
3), and `$count` counts the items of a sequence — a string is one item, so it
answers 1. Neither is Python's `len(s)`. The length in code points is
`strings:length`.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings' as=strings]
[r count=[$count 'banana'] needle=[$strings:count 'banana' 'a']]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r count=1 needle=3]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-string-length-right level=core
  [title [#`strings:length`#]]
  [tags strings length count python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings' as=strings]
[r length=[$strings:length 'banana']]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r length=6]
#]]
