 ]

 [; ── P18. coming from Python: int-division (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-int-division-wrong level=core
  [title [#`/` for an integer result#]]
  [tags arithmetic division idiv int float python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
`/` is true division. Over two ints it answers an int only when the
quotient is whole; otherwise a float (`[/ 7 2]` is `3.5e0`) — never Python
2's floor. Integer division is `[$idiv a b]` (truncating toward zero) and the
remainder is `[% a b]`.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[r half=[/ 7 2] even=[/ 6 2]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r half=3.5e0 even=3]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-int-division-right level=core
  [title [#`[$idiv a b]` for the quotient, `[% a b]` for the remainder#]]
  [tags arithmetic division idiv int float python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[r quot=[$idiv 7 2] rem=[% 7 2]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[r quot=3 rem=1]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]

 [; ── P19. coming from Python: brackets (issue 1813 §27) ── ]

 [case id=ap-py-brackets-wrong level=core
  [title [#Miscounted closing brackets#]]
  [tags brackets fmt lint parse python antipattern gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [why [#
Every form closes with its own `]`, and a long one-line program is where a
count goes wrong. CX refuses a stray `]` or an unclosed `[` at parse, naming
the line and column, before anything runs. Do not count by eye: `cx fmt FILE`
prints the program in canonical layout (indent 2, width 80, a form too wide
broken across lines) so each closer sits at the end of its form, and refuses
the same miscount at the same column; `cx lint FILE` checks without printing.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $xs (1, 2, 3)] [report total=[?reduce $xs [using [?fn ($acc $x) [+ $acc $x]]] [init 0]]]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
error: cx-err:CXER0100: parse: unmatched `]` — no open `[` for this closer (a stray `]`, or one `]` too many on a construct that already closed) at line 1:99
#]]
  [exit-code [#1#]]
 ]

 [case id=ap-py-brackets-right level=core
  [title [#Let `cx fmt` lay the program out#]]
  [tags brackets fmt lint parse python gaps-1 issue-1813]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?let [= $xs (1, 2, 3)] [report total=[?reduce $xs [using [?fn ($acc $x) [+ $acc $x]]] [init 0]]]]
#]]
  [cli-argv [#
fmt
%FILE%
#]]
  [out-text [#
[?let [= $xs (1, 2, 3)]
  [report total=[?reduce $xs [using [?fn ($acc $x) [+ $acc $x]]] [init 0]]]]
#]]
  [exit-code [#0#]]
 ]
]
